hadiths[30]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1175","Yunus bin Jubair said:\I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So he said: 'Don't you know Abdullah bin Umar?' Indeed he divorced his wife while she was menstruating"""""
"1176","Salim narrated that:His father divorced his wife during her menses"
"1177","Narrated by Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), who reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\No woman harms her husband in this worldly life except that his wife among the *Hoor al-'Een* (companions of Paradise) says: 'Do not harm him! May Allah fight you! He is merely a guest (*dakheel*) in your company"
"1178","Narrated Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, narrated Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, who said: I asked Ibn 'Umar رضي الله عنهما about a man who divorced his wife while she was in a state of menstruation. He said: \Do you know 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar? He divorced his wife while she was in a state of menstruation"
"1179","Fatimah bint Qais said:\My husband divorced me three times during the time of the Prophet. So the Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no housing for you nor maintenance.'\"" Al-Mughirah (one of the narrators) said: \""I mentioned that to Ibrahim and he said: Umar said: \""We do not leave the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of our Prophet for the saying of a woman"""""
"1180","Hannād narrated to us: Qabīṣah narrated to us, from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim, from al-Zubayr ibn Saʿīd, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said:\n\n\I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said"
"1181","Muzahir bin Aslam narrated that Al-Qasim narrated from Aishah that:The Messenger of Allah said: \The divorce for a slave woman is two divorces"""""
"1182","Abu Hurairah narraed that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Allah has permitted my Ummah what occurs in their mines"""""
"1183","Hannad narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us; from al-Mughirah; from al-Sha‘bi, who said: Fatimah bint Qays said: My husband divorced me thrice (irrevocably) during the time of the Prophet (ﷺ), so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no lodging for you and no maintenance."" Al-Mughirah said: I mentioned it to Ibrahim, so he said: ‘Umar said: ""We do not abandon the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of our Prophet (ﷺ) for the saying of a woman whom we do not know whether she remembered or forgot."" And ‘Umar used to assign her lodging and maintenance. Ahmad ibn Mani‘ narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; he informed us: Husayn, Isma‘il, and Mujalid. Hushaym said: And Dawud also narrated to us from al-Sha‘bi. He said: I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) concerning her. She said: Her husband divorced her irrevocably (al-battah), so she disputed with him over lodging and maintenance, and the Prophet (ﷺ) did not assign her lodging or maintenance. In the hadith of Dawud, she said: ""And he commanded me to observe my ‘iddah in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."" Abu ‘Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith. And it is the saying of some people of knowledge, among them al-Hasan al-Basri, ‘Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, and al-Sha‘bi. And this is the saying of Ahmad and Ishaq. They said: There is no lodging and no maintenance for the divorced woman if her husband does not possess the right of return (raj‘ah). And some people of knowledge from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), among them ‘Umar and ‘Abdullah, said: The thrice-divorced woman has lodging and maintenance. This is the saying of Sufyan al-Thawri and the people of Kufa. And some people of knowledge said: She has lodging but no maintenance. This is the saying of Malik ibn Anas, al-Layth ibn Sa‘d, and al-Shafi‘i. Al-Shafi‘i said: We only assigned her lodging by the Book of Allah. Allah the Exalted said: (Do not turn them out of their houses, nor shall they leave, unless they commit a clear indecency). They said: It is foul speech (al-badha’), that she speaks foully to her family. He argued that the Prophet (ﷺ) did not assign Fatimah bint Qays lodging because she used to speak foully to her family. Al-Shafi‘i said: And she has no maintenance due to the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the story of Fatimah bint Qays."
"1184","AR-Rubayyi bint Mu'awwidh bin Al-Afra narrated:that she got a Khul during the time of the Prophet. So the Prophet ordered her - or: she was ordered - that she observe an Iddah of a menstruation"
"1185","Yunus bin Jubair said:\I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So he said: 'Don't you know Abdullah bin Umar?' Indeed he divorced his wife while she was menstruating"""""
"1186","Thawban narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: \Whichever woman seeks a Khul from her husband without harm (cause)"""""
"1187","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Indeed the woman is like a rib"""""
"1188","Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān, who reported from al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā, from Sufyān, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the freed slave of the family of Ṭalḥah, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh ibn ʿAfrāʾ (may Allāh be pleased with her), that she sought a *khulʿ* (divorce initiated by the wife) during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ commanded her — or she was commanded — to observe her *ʿiddah* (waiting period) with one menstrual cycle.\n\nHe (Abū ʿĪsā) said: \In this chapter"
"1189","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: \No woman should ask for the divorce of her sister (in religion) in order to spill what is in her container"""""
"1190","Abu Hurairah narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: \Every divorce is valid except the divorce of the Ma'tuh person whose reason is overcome.\"" (Da'if Jiddan)"""""
"1191","Bundār informed us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Ayyūb informed us from Abū Qilābah, from the one who narrated to him from Thawbān رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n> \Any woman who asks her husband for a divorce without any valid cause"
"1192","Al-Aswad narrated from Abu As-Sanabil bin Ba'kak who said:\Subai'ah delivered twenty-three or twenty-five days after her husband had died. So when she was ready (finished post-natal bleeding) she adorned herself for marriage"""""
"1193","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad, that he was informed by Ibn al-Mubarak, who was informed by Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Hamzah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\n*\There was a woman under my marriage whom I loved"
"1194","Humaid bin Nafi narrated that :Zainab bint Abi Salamah said: \I entered upon Umm Habibah"""""
"1195","Humaid bin Nafi narrated that :Zainab said: \So I entered upon Zainab bint Jahsh when her brother died. She called for some perfume and put it on"""""
"1196","Humaid bin Nafi narrated that :Zainab said: ""So I entered upon Zainab bint Jahsh when her brother died. She called for some perfume and put it on, then said: 'By Allah! I have no need for perfume except that I heard the Messenger of Allah said: ""It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for the dead more than three nights, except for her husband (in which case it is) four months and ten days"
"1197","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Mani', narrated to us Husayn ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Shayban, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak, who said:\n\nSubay'a gave birth twenty-three or twenty-five days after the death of her husband. When she had recovered (from childbirth), she adorned herself for marriage, and this was disapproved of. The matter was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \If she does so"
"1198","Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that Abū Hurayrah, Ibn ʿAbbās, and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān discussed the matter of a pregnant woman whose husband had passed away and she gave birth at the time of her husband's death.\n\nIbn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \She must observe the longer of the two waiting periods (*ʿiddah*).\""\n\nAbū Salamah"
"1199","Abu Salamah and Muhammad bin Abdur-Rahman (bin Thawban) narrated that :Salman bin Sakhr Al-Ansari - from Banu Bayadah - said that his wife was like the back of his mother to him until Ramadan passed. After half of Ramadan had passed he had intercourse with his wife during the night. So he went to the Messenger of Allah to mention that to him. The Messenger of Allah said to him: \Free a slave.\"" He said: \""I don't have one.\"" So he said: \""Then fast two consecutive months.\"" He said: \""I am unable.\"" He said: \""Feed sixty needy people.\"" He said: \""I can not.\"" So the Messenger of Allah said to Farwah bin Amr: \""Give him that Araq - and it is a large basket that holds fifteen or sixteen Sa - to feed sixty needy people"""""
"1200","Aishah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah swore Ila from his wives"""""
"1201","Sa'eed bin Jubair narrated:\I was asked about those who were involved in the case of Li'an and if they are to be separated"""""
"1202","Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Salamah ibn Ṣakhr al-Bayāḍī, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding the one who commits ẓihār and then has intercourse before expiating, he said: \A single expiation.\"" Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith. The practice according to this is held by the majority of the scholars"
"1203","Zainab bint Ka'b bin Ujrah narrated that :Al-Furay'ah bint Malik bin Sinan - the sister of the Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri - informed her that she went to the Messenger of Allah to ask him if she could return to her family in Banu Khudrah. Her husband had gone out searching for his runaway slaves"
"1204","Ibn Mas'ud narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the one who consumed Riba"""""
